      "message": "eng a11y note: ensure the \"X\" button is labeled as \"Close\"\n\nNote: While a button does not have any visible text always, NVDA will not read the label, which is a known issue with NVDA mouse tracking. The button still should have an accessible name provided (which can be checked in the Devtools Accessibility inspector or by `tab`bing to the button with NVDA). [Editing to add: QA would likely flag it because it is a suboptimal user experience, even thought it is a screen reader bug].\n\nWhat we could do to make the user experience more delightful is to add an invisible `<span>` in the button as Calixte offered in the bug 1886964#c1 and in the attached patch. This would also work as an accessible name source for the button.",
